{"availability":"available","full":"orhun/tuitar","name":"tuitar","description":"A portable guitar training tool & DIY kit 🎛️🎸","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":530,"forks":19,"created":"2025-05-21T21:24:36Z","updated":"2025-12-23T07:48:43Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://orhun.dev/tuitar/","topics":["fretboard","guitar","instrument","ratatui","rust","training","tuning","visualization"],"demo":"https://rustforgeconf.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:27:57.623Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T00:27:57.623Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T00:27:57.623Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:03.356Z","stars":530,"forks":19},{"at":"2026-10-08T00:27:57.623Z","stars":530,"forks":19}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Learning how to play guitar with a TUI - hence \"Tuitar\".","Tuitar is a terminal-based guitar training tool that runs standalone on ESP32 hardware. Available as a DIY kit, see the firmware and hardware sections for more details.","Tuitar is currently in prototype stage but you can still try it out and contribute to the project. The plan is to feature it on CrowdSupply once the firmware and hardware are stable. Let me know if you are interested in supporting the project or have any feedback! All of this is built on livestream as a part of a series called Becoming a Musician (100+ hours of content!) Follow @tuitardev on X (Twitter) to not miss any updates!"],"features":["Jump to the features ➡️","Frequency/Spectrum/Waveform","License & Contributions","Tuitar offers real-time visualizations from an input source which can be used for tuning your guitar or other instruments.","The frequency graph above shows the detected frequency of the input sound. When a fundamental frequency is detected, the closest musical note is being displayed with the respective cents>) with a bar at the top."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orhun/tuitar/blob/main